\cf2 \cb7 \strokec2 Overall explanation
\f1 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 Correct option:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb7 Applying multiple layers of security measures including input validation, access controls, and continuous monitoring to address vulnerabilities
\f1\b0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 Architecting a defense-in-depth security approach involves implementing multiple layers of security to protect generative AI applications. This includes input validation to prevent malicious data inputs, strict access controls to limit who can interact with the AI models, and continuous monitoring to detect and respond to security incidents. These measures can help address common vulnerabilities and meet the best practices for securing generative AI applications on AWS.\cb1 \
\cb7 Incorrect options:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb7 Implementing a single-layer firewall to block unauthorized access to the AI models
\f1\b0 \'a0- While a firewall is an important security measure, relying on a single layer of defense is insufficient for comprehensive security. Defense-in-depth requires multiple, overlapping layers of protection.\cb1 \

\f3\b \cb7 Relying solely on data encryption to protect the AI training data
\f1\b0 \'a0- Data encryption is crucial for protecting data at rest and in transit, but it does not address other vulnerabilities such as input validation or unauthorized access. A holistic security strategy is needed.\cb1 \

\f3\b \cb7 Using a single authentication mechanism for all users and services accessing the AI models
\f1\b0 \'a0- Employing a single authentication mechanism is a weak security practice. Multiple authentication and authorization mechanisms should be used to ensure robust access control.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
