\f1 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 A healthcare startup is developing a machine learning model to predict patient outcomes based on historical medical data. During the training process, the data science team notices signs of overfitting, where the model performs well on the training data but struggles with new, unseen data. To ensure the model generalizes effectively and avoids memorizing the training data, the team needs to implement strategies to prevent overfitting.\cb1 \
\cb3 How can you prevent model-overfitting in machine learning?\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf6 \cb7 \strokec6 By avoiding any form of model validation or testing to prevent the model from learning incorrect patterns\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf8 \strokec8 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf2 \cb12 \strokec2 By using techniques such as cross-validation, regularization, and pruning to simplify the model and improve its generalization\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf6 \cb7 \strokec6 By increasing the complexity of the model to ensure it captures all nuances in the training data\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf6 \cb7 \strokec6 By only training the model on a small subset of the available data to reduce the amount of information it has to learn\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 \strokec2 Overall explanation
\f1 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 Correct option:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb7 By using techniques such as cross-validation, regularization, and pruning to simplify the model and improve its generalization
\f1\b0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 To prevent overfitting, techniques such as cross-validation, regularization, and pruning are employed. Cross-validation helps ensure the model generalizes well to unseen data by dividing the data into multiple training and validation sets. Regularization techniques, such as L1 and L2 regularization, penalize complex models to reduce overfitting. Pruning simplifies decision trees by removing branches that have little importance.\cb1 \
\
